  "chief_complaint": "Advanced chronic kidney disease (stage 4) with proteinuric diabetic nephropathy and pending kidney transplantation",
  "history_of_present_illness": "The patient has experienced a progressive decline in renal function over the past nine years, advancing from CKD stage 1 in 2017 to stage 4 in 2025. Diabetic kidney disease is evident by microalbuminuria in 2018, evolving to overt proteinuria in 2024. Hypertension, treated with three agents, has been refractory, and anemia requiring epoetin alfa has developed. Metabolic syndrome, obesity, smoking, and heavy alcohol use further accelerate renal and cardiovascular risk. The patient is awaiting kidney transplantation and is on insulin therapy despite only a prediabetes label, indicating overt type 2 diabetes. Additional comorbidities include osteoporosis, osteoarthritis, hypothyroidism, and psychosocial stressors (intimate\u2011partner abuse, chronic stress). Polypharmacy (9 agents) and use of naproxen in stage\u202f14 CKD raise safety concerns.",
